Far, far beyond the rolling billows Faith spreads her wings;
Love tells us of the golden City, Hope of its glory sings.
There shall sorrow, pain, and parting Grieve our hearts no more;
Soon, soon we‘ll meet beyond the river, Safe on the Homeland shore.

Far, far beyond the vale and shadow Loved ones have pass‘d;
