O blessed morn of joy unbounded! O glorious day!
There ev‘ry tear of grief and anguish Jesus shall wipe away.
There shall sorrow, pain, and parting Grieve our hearts no more;
Soon, soon we‘ll meet beyond the river, Safe on the Homeland shore.

Grace! ‘tis a charming sound, Harmonious to mine ear;
Heav’n with the echo shall resound,
And all the earth shall hear.

Grace first contrived the way To save rebellious man;
And all the steps that grace display
First drew the Wondrous plan.

Grace led my roving feet To tread the heav’nly road;
And new supplies each hour I meet,
While pressing on to God.

Grace all the work shall crown, Thro‘ everlasting days;
It lays in heav‘n the topmoststone,
And well deserves the praise.

Think and reflect; God prepares a land so bless‘d.
Leave your sins and come find strength in hope for heaven’s rest.
Why be sinless? Why be pure thus? Think and reflect;
Heav’n is holy, heav’n is lovely, blessings o’erflow;
I will ever struggle to reach that Home.

Think and reflect; Jesus shares a land that‘s bless‘d.
Hold your faith and seek His favor; hope for heaven’s rest.
Why be selfless? Why seek Jesus? Think and reflect;
Heav’n is endless, heav’n is spacious, boundless and free;
I will ever strive for my Home to see.

Think and reflect, on the Holy Spirit bless‘d.
For His dear love follow Him, then; hope for heaven’s rest.
Why seek His Way? Why must we pray? Think and reflect;
Heav’n is splendour, heav‘n is treasure, precious and rare;
I will ever run to my promise there.

I’ve reached the land of corn and wine, And all its riches freely mine;
Here shines undimmed one blissful day, For all my night has passed away.
O Beulah Land, sweet Beulah Land, As on thy highest mount I stand;
I look away across the sea, Where mansions are prepared for me,
And view the shining glory shore: My heaven, my home forevermore!

My Saviour comes and walks with me, And sweet communion here have we;
